ical':..}`). Fix: read `raw['canonical']` first and match `arkitscenes/`, then test on c1_row-shaped rows. The fix changes loader_audit.py, so rebind and re-seal the selection fingerprint. Nothing gates on this census, so it fails silently rather than closed.\n2. MEDIUM, provenance. Three archives share the name p_1130b378.tar and identity 782f303d: snapshot 42bbcbb2, live 21e1ec60, and my rebuild from the snapshot's sources, a9bd0b77. They differ only in u.py (tools/unit_binding.py) and sums.txt. t.tar and every other member are byte-equal, and the tree equals the archive's. The config identity does not cover u.py, and no proof path calls u.py (jb.sh, s.sh, p.py, p_125c4c87.sh). snap_782f303d is not a clean freeze: its rebind.py, unit_binding.py and test_packet.py are dated 16:25Z, after its FIX5.md and tests.log (16:23Z), and hold half-finished item-4 code. Its sources therefore cannot rebuild its archive, and its suite gives 27/28 (KeyError s1_routing.py in the packing test). The live copy passes 28/28. Fix: the proof submission names the archive SHA it uses.\n3. PASS, finding 1 of the first review. p.py:262-263 calls temporary_paths after command(), and :288-290 fails the receipt unless all eight checks are present and PASS. s.sh:37-38 asserts each of the eight. test_main_builds_receipt_with_all_evaluated_checks passes in both copies: it runs the real main(), calls temporary_paths once and writes eight PASS checks. Its fixture mocks command(), program() and execute(), and it fabricates the four checks the audit supplies.\n4. PASS, v7 binding. rows.sqlite hashes to 210b2534 and receipt.json to 8091154c. The archive's d.json (4e539365) pins d.db 210b2534 and the receipt copy 8091154c, and config streams.vqa pins that d.json. My recount over all 204,413 rows: 431 traced room rows (pool r1_room_traced), all admitted by room_trace. away_opp has 8,511 rows (easy 3,664, medium 2,665, hard 2,182), all with facing=away. Direction (49,901) and counting (11,366) equal the first review's counts; facing 43,469 = 34,958 + 8,511. Size is 0 and direction 3,117 = 3,289 - 172. Room 172 = cap 431*4*100//1000. Rerunning the packet's main rebind reproduces 782f303d and run key 125c4c87. Each fallback ran as one command with rc=0. Room 0 gives room 0 and direction 3,289 (identity cfdb1b00). Away excluded gives facing eligible 34,958 with 8,511 excluded (identity 3d056b29).\n5. PASS, room predicate. It admits 431/431 traced rows. It refuses all 571 one-line rows, even with pool forced to r1_room_traced. It refuses all 431 rows under each of my 15 mutants: frame 33, frame 0, no relation, two relations, digit or spelled number, area line, wrong pool, bad pin, no Seen line, non-numeric answer, trailing text, no relation keyword, leading Locate line, extra digit in a Seen line. ground_rows, s1_pool, s1_admission, s1_routing and s1_exclusions are byte-equal to b01ce449. Against snap_841f0637, the tree differs only in type_mix, vehicle_p and loader_audit.\n6. PASS, units. Units are unbound at 0 cents and listed under absent_on_P. Units under 100 go to missing_units and absent_on_P, not to missing. The allowlist defaults to ft. dose = min(cents, 4*eligible*100//1000), and the rest of the 6,400 cents goes pro rata to the four program cells, by largest remainders. Item 4 is off unless --pack-unit-slice is given with four pins. pack_slice adds only events and frame pins and refuses a changed answer (test). The s1_routing SHA 5c8cd973 it hard-codes equals b01ce449's. FIX5 and R1P_PACKET now name units_p_slice_v3 (747 rows: ft 683, in 64), per ORCH NOTE 1605Z.\n7. PASS, names. The loader audit runs as `$PILOT_VENV/bin/python -B - $X` with X=$AS/ap/$K, and its code arrives by heredoc. All new names are opaque hex (p_125c4c87.sh, i_/x_1130b378, ap/1130b378/{c,d,r,s,v}.json, s_22b44165, a15_cot_ap125c4c87). The one name with a project word, benchmark_scene_exclusions.json, is inherited (H1 fx/k, 841f0637).\n8. PASS, selection. Against FIX3's 88bd3399, r.json differs only in the implementation fingerprints of type_mix.py and vehicle_p.py (fix 4) and loader_audit.py (fix 5). s1_pool.implementation() equals r.json on 841f0637, a6b70ef2 and 782f303d. q.json reports non_room_equal, 586 removed and 82,598 selected. Against 841f0637, the config differs only in identity and run pins, the vqa store (v6 to v7), room 172 / direction 3,117, units_allowlist [ft] and exclude_qid_suffix null. Routing cells and every other entry are unchanged. I did not recheck d07c3bd5, which FIX3 superseded.\n9. LOW. With units bound, absent_on_p names only units under 100. An allowlist-excluded unit with 100 or more rows would go undrawn without being named; harmless now that in has 64 rows. s.sh gates with Python `assert` under plain `python3 -B`, so PYTHONOPTIMIZE in the operator's environment would disable every gate (inherited pattern; `-I` or explicit raises would close it).\nNot checked: Orchard staging, real RGB, production routing populations, the v3 half-extent clearance itself.\n", 'r3.txt': "# REVIEW_VERDICT_R1P3: GO (archive p_c5f3847d.tar sha256 888027436a99cfec360959c46f4271222e4c029f5d36eb9870fea4f669231029; config d8b03fd14db01af4def4a0cfd9a49d16ec492d9a3c6b0c56977f7f22b79f705a; run key 26cc98b7)\nReviewer: review_r1p3 (Devin, Claude Opus), trinity-1-3, 17:08-17:18Z. Evidence: /scratch/jjyeung/orch_n30/review_r1p3/work (f6 = snap_f719b05f copy, f7 = r1_pkt copy 17:10:39Z, SHA256SUMS OK for both; ar5/ar6/ar7 extracted archives; gprobe.py, prefix_probe.py, tests_*.log, fb7_main).\nBefore the Orchard proof, the drivers must be repinned to the new identity (finding 7). That step changes no packet code.\n1. PASS, fix 6 deriver. validate_evidence uses only g.read_pin/identity/digest and d.contract. On the deriver's READY kit, inherited g.check(kit,{},'p') passes when only persistent_launch is stubbed. Across 15 evidence mutants plus a re-pin without cfg.admission, g.check and the deriver refuse the same 15, and the deriver also refuses a foreign 4.json config_sha256 that g.check accepts. The deriver omits g.check's slot, version and source-seal predicates. Those predicates bind packet and H bytes, not evidence, and g.check accepts the derived kit. The deriver needs no SLURM variable. The test's audit hook and its r8/persistent_launch profile guard both pass in my copy. The modules it loads (g, i, v, q0, d) have no side effects at import, and the deriver sets dont_write_bytecode.\n2. PASS, fix 6 job path. f719b05f differs from snapshot 42bbcbb2 only in d.py, u.py and sums.txt. u.py (c376dc31) equals the live fix-5 u.py that review_r1p2 reviewed. BASE_RUNTIME and the path substitution are unchanged, and the test's b/ and job.sh files are byte-equal. job.sh:16 still runs `python3 -I b/g.py $ROOT p` in the job environment before r8 and r.sh.\n3. PASS, fix 7 census. I ran 4 datasets x 4 scenes through the packet's c1_row (sha 6da7cebc, JSON round-tripped, no top-level provenance). The fix-7 loader gives the exact prefixes scannetpp/, scannetppv2/, scannet/ and arkitscenes/; the fix-6 loader gives 16/16 unknown. The test builds its rows with the same frozen c1_row.\n4. PASS, fix 7 threshold. 1/100 and 10/1000 PASS; 2/100, 11/1000 and 1/1 FAIL. A FAIL sets a.json to FAIL and raises. p.py requires all 8 checks PASS, and s.sh asserts loader_audit PASS. 0/0 passes this check, but absolute_distance is a required routing family (vehicle_p.ROUTING), so the family gate catches it.\n5. PASS, PYTHONOPTIMIZE. s.sh runs `env -u PYTHONOPTIMIZE python3 -I -B -`. My probe with PYTHONOPTIMIZE=2: `python -I -c 'assert False'` exits rc=1, and without -I it exits rc=0. The proof script and every jb.sh python call also use -I.\n6. PASS, scope. ground_rows, s1_pool, s1_admission, s1_routing and s1_exclusions are byte-equal to b01ce449. The trees differ from f719b05f only in loader_audit.py. d.py, p.py, q.py, qp.py, v.py, u.py and b0.json are unchanged. jb.sh and the proof script differ only by store and run key. s.sh differs by